17592186097775 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186097776 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097775 #edb/ref 1061 618389 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097775 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "333f87c0-71a4-538e-9783-f364abf0caa7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097775 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186096834 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097776 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186097777 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097776 #edb/ref 1061 618392 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097776 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "fdfdcd42-ada8-5eea-ae27-e68cd87d7470" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097776 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186096835 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097777 #edb/ref 1061 618395 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097777 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c0d6168f-5f91-5b54-9679-17a077751add" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097777 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186096836 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097927 #edb/ref 1064 "Suppose that we want to evaluate the integral\n\n$$\n\\int x\\ln{x}\\, \\textrm{d}x \\,.\n$$\n\nThe method of integration by parts can help us solve this problem. Let's remind ourselves of the \"by-parts\" formula,\n\n$$\n\\int u v' \\textrm{d}x = uv - \\int v u'\\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe usually let $u = x,$ but that would leave us with $v' = \\ln(x)$ which is hard to integrate. So instead, we're going to choose our $u$ and $v'$ slightly differently, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow the formula of integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}_{⏟}}_{u}\\cdot {{x}_{⏟}}_{{v}^{′}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,{x}^{2}-\\int \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\,{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\frac{1}{2}\\int x\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\,{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen we apply integration by parts to integrals containing logarithmic functions, we should *always* identify the logarithmic function with $u,$ not with $v'.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097927 #edb/ref 1065 897 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097927 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "dbf22d18-c638-527f-a085-8fcc19fbfbeb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097927 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175901 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049593 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175901 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186176493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175901 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186176497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175901 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186234352 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175901 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186266042 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175901 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186266043 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175901 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186266044 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175901 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186266059 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175901 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186329840 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175901 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186341990 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175901 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186341991 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175901 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186341993 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175901 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186341994 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175901 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186342003 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175901 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186508954 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175901 #edb/ref 1039 "Applying the Extreme Value Theorem to Piecewise Functions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175901 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186175768 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175901 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "eede91c4-9099-55df-a803-f87895d9f51b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175902 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049162 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186175902 #edb/